    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The M 260 utilizes a highly complex simplex timing chain system situated between the engine and the transmission. This rear placement makes any timing service an absolute nightmare. Accessing the timing components requires physically dropping the entire engine and front subframe out of the vehicle, turning preventative maintenance into a massive, multi-day labor job. The chain is subjected to immense stress under the AMG's 400 Nm of torque.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection (Features a highly advanced Bosch high-pressure direct injection system operating at 250 bar. The Piezo injectors optimize spray, providing phenomenal fuel atomization but guaranteeing severe intake valve carbon buildup. Professional Walnut Blasting is required every 60,000 miles to restore airflow and prevent misfires. The High-Pressure Fuel Pump is driven directly by the camshaft and must flow immense volumes of fuel.)",
    engineLifespan: "100,000 - 150,000+ miles (The mechanical core is an exceptionally robust die-cast aluminum block featuring Nanoslide bore spray coating. However, because this is an AMG model, it is frequently driven extremely hard and subjected to intense thermal loads. Early 2019-2020 models suffer from a catastrophic cylinder head defect that drastically shortens lifespan if not fixed under warranty. Lifespan is highly dependent on obsessive 6,000-mile oil changes and strict transmission maintenance.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Intercooled. Equipped with a massive twin-scroll turbocharger featuring an electronic wastegate actuator. The twin-scroll design perfectly separates exhaust pulses, drastically reducing turbo lag. Because the A 35 pushes 302hp, the turbo operates near its thermal limits. Proper warm-up and cool-down procedures are absolutely mandatory to prevent oil coking in the bearings. The mechanical linkage rod connecting the actuator to the wastegate flap wears out over time.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.7 (A highly complex engine management system overseeing direct injection, electronic boost control, CAMTRONIC variable valve lift, and the thermal module. The USA Spec ECU is mapped for EPA emissions and lacks the restrictive European GPF logic, delivering sharp throttle response and loud exhaust pops on overrun. It is incredibly receptive to OBD2 flashing, allowing tuners to safely extract massive power.)",
    euroStandard: "ULEV / EPA (No GPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "360 - 380 hp (The stock internals handle 360 horsepower effortlessly. A Stage 1 tune safely unlocks massive mid-range torque on US 91/93 octane fuel. Pushing beyond 380hp requires a larger hybrid turbocharger, an upgraded intercooler, and a high-flow downpipe, at which point the AMG Speedshift 7G-DCT transmission's internal wet clutch packs become the primary, fragile limiting factor.)",
    fuelConsumption: {
      city: "11.0 - 13.0 L/100km",
      highway: "7.5 - 9.0 L/100km",
      mixed: "9.0 - 10.5 L/100km",
      sporty: "15.0+ L/100km"
    },
    oilSpecification: "0W-20 or 5W-40 Synthetic (MB 229.5 or MB 229.71 depending on exact spec and climate)",
    commonIssues: [
      "Cylinder Head Exhaust Valve Seat Failure (2019-2020 Models): The absolute most critical and catastrophic flaw of early A 35 models. A manufacturing defect causes the exhaust valve seats to prematurely recede deep into the aluminum cylinder head. This results in a total loss of compression, severe cold-start misfires, rough idling, and illuminating the Check Engine Light. The only fix is replacing the entire cylinder head assembly.",
      "Thermal Management Module Failure: The M 260 abandons traditional thermostats for a highly complex, electronically controlled rotary valve module that directs coolant. The internal plastic gears wear out or the electric motor burns out, causing the valve to jam. This leads to severe overheating, requiring an expensive module replacement.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Rattle: The timing chain is located at the back of the engine. The hydraulic tensioner frequently degrades under the massive AMG torque, causing the chain to slap against the plastic guides on cold starts. Ignoring this rattle risks the chain jumping teeth, and repairing it requires dropping the entire engine out of the car.",
      "AMG Speedshift 7G-DCT Contamination: The 400 Nm of torque generates immense friction material from the wet clutch packs during aggressive Race Starts (Launch Control). If the transmission fluid and filters are not changed strictly every 40,000 miles, the metallic debris clogs the Mechatronic unit, resulting in harsh gear engagements and eventual failure.",
      "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Due to the high-pressure direct injection entirely bypassing the intake valves, PCV oil vapor bakes into a thick, sticky carbon sludge on the hot valve stems. This heavily restricts airflow, causing rough cold idles, severe hesitation, and dangerous high-RPM misfires until professionally Walnut Blasted.",
      "Electronic Wastegate Rattle: The mechanical linkage rod connecting the electronic actuator to the massive twin-scroll turbocharger wastegate flap wears out prematurely from extreme heat cycling. This causes a distinct, loud metallic rattle during deceleration.",
      "4MATIC PTU/Rear Differential Wear: The all-wheel-drive system is heavily stressed during aggressive launches. Neglecting fluid changes in the rear differential and the Power Transfer Unit (PTU) will cause the clutch packs to burn out, leading to binding or a total loss of AWD capability."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Catastrophic Engine Failure (Cylinder Head Defect): If you buy a 2019-2020 model that has not had its cylinder head replaced under warranty, you are holding a ticking financial time bomb. When the valve seats recede and compression is lost, the repair bill for a new cylinder head and labor routinely exceeds $6,000 USD.",
      "Economic Total Loss (Rear Chain Labor): Because the timing chain is wedged against the firewall, fixing a worn chain or shattered guides requires physically unbolting and dropping the entire engine and front subframe out of the vehicle. This turns a routine repair into a massive, multi-day labor nightmare costing thousands of dollars.",
      "Economic Total Loss (DCT Mechatronic Failure): Neglecting the AMG Speedshift 7G-DCT fluid changes or abusing Launch Control will relentlessly destroy the internal wet clutch pack and the highly sensitive Mechatronic control unit. A full transmission rebuild easily costs upwards of $4,000 USD.",
      "Cylinder Head Warping (Thermal Module Jam): If the complex rotary thermal management module jams closed, the engine will dump its coolant or block flow to the radiator. The ultra-modern, lightweight aluminum block will warp and crack incredibly fast if the driver attempts to keep driving while overheating.",
      "Drivability Loss (Carbon Choking): Severe carbon and oil sludge buildup on the intake valves will eventually restrict airflow so heavily that the engine physically cannot breathe at higher RPMs. The engine will suffer from random cylinder misfires, incredibly poor acceleration, and will force the ECU into Limp Mode.",
      "Ignition Coil Melt (Ignored Spark Plugs): If the delicate spark plugs are left in past their 40,000-mile service life, the immense boost pressure forces the ignition coils to work significantly harder to jump the gap. This eventually causes the coils to overheat, melt internally, and leave the driver stranded."
    ],
