    yearRange: "2019-present",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The M 139 utilizes a massively upgraded, heavy-duty timing chain system compared to standard models, designed specifically to withstand the immense 500 Nm of torque and 7200 RPM redline of the 'S' variant. While catastrophic chain snapping is exceptionally rare, the hydraulic tensioners are still subjected to extreme thermal loads and can degrade. Crucially, the rear-mounted location against the firewall means that any timing-related service dictates that the entire engine and transmission assembly must be physically removed from the vehicle. This turns any timing repair into an astronomical, multi-day labor nightmare.)",
    injectionType: "Dual Stage Injection (Direct + Port Injection). (This is the defining reliability upgrade of the M139 over standard Mercedes engines. It features a highly sophisticated two-stage system: high-pressure Piezo injectors (200 bar) spray directly into the cylinders, while secondary solenoid injectors spray into the intake manifold. This dual-injection setup brillianty serves a dual purpose: it flows enough fuel to support the massive 421hp output, and the port injectors continuously wash the intake valves with raw fuel. This completely eliminates the severe carbon choking issues that plague standard direct-injected Mercedes engines. No Walnut Blasting is required.)",
    engineLifespan: "150,000 - 250,000+ km (The M 139 is an entirely hand-built masterpiece from Affalterbach, following the 'One Man, One Engine' philosophy. The closed-deck aluminum block features chill-cast construction and forged internals, making it structurally capable of withstanding immense boost pressures. However, because it produces a staggering 211hp per liter, it operates at the absolute physical limits of 2.0L thermal dynamics. The lifespan is entirely dependent on meticulous, obsessive maintenance. The extreme ambient heat in the engine bay rapidly bakes all plastic cooling lines and wiring harnesses, causing them to become brittle and fail.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Intercooled. Equipped with a colossal, highly specialized twin-scroll turbocharger featuring roller bearings for insanely fast spooling despite its size. Mercedes drastically re-engineered the M139 by rotating the engine 180 degrees; the intake is now at the front, and the massive turbocharger sits at the rear firewall. This optimizes aerodynamics but completely cooks the firewall area. The turbo in the 'S' model runs an astonishing 2.1 bar (30.5 psi) of boost. It is cooled by a dedicated electric water pump that continues running after the engine is shut off to prevent the oil from coking inside the ultra-expensive roller bearings.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.8 (A highly sophisticated, bespoke AMG engine management system. It meticulously controls the massive 2.1 bar boost pressure, the dual-stage injection transition, and interfaces perfectly with the 8-speed AMG Speedshift DCT to execute violent, lightning-fast gear changes and aggressive rev-matching. Despite already producing 421hp, the M 139 is incredibly receptive to aftermarket tuning. However, tuning an engine already operating at this level of thermal stress requires extreme caution and absolute adherence to high-octane premium fuel to prevent catastrophic detonation.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d (Equipped with GPF - Gasoline Particulate Filter)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "480 - 520 hp (The M 139 features a closed-deck aluminum block, forged crankshaft, and forged pistons directly from the factory. The internals are phenomenally strong. A Stage 1 tune easily pushes the engine past 460 horsepower. Pushing beyond 500hp requires an upgraded downpipe and a high-performance intercooler. The ultimate limiting factor is not the engine block, but rather the immense heat soak, the flow limit of the factory turbocharger, and the physical torque limits of the 8-speed AMG DCT clutches during Launch Control.)",
